## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests the ability to design a dynamic programming solution for array partitioning with a per-segment objective function. It combines partition DP with range maximum queries and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic programming over array partitions
- Range maximum queries (precomputation table M[a][b])
- Path reconstruction using parent pointers
- Time/space complexity: O(n²k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPartition(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length-1; // 1-indexed array
  const M = Array.from({length:n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));

  // Precompute range maximums
  for(let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    M[i][i] = A[i];
    for(let j=i+1; j<=n; j++){
      M[i][j] = Math.max(M[i][j-1], A[j]);
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for(let t=1; t<=k; t++){
    for(let i=t; i<=n; i++){
      for(let j=t-1; j<i; j++){
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + M[j+1][i] - c;
        if(val > dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = val;
          par[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct segments
  const segments = [];
  let curr = n;
  for(let t=k; t>=1; t--){
    const prev = par[curr][t];
    segments.unshift([prev+1, curr]);
    curr = prev;
  }

  return {value: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

## Optimization Opportunities
- Use sparse table for O(1) range max queries with O(n log n) preprocessing
- Apply divide and conquer optimization if applicable
- Consider rolling array optimization to reduce space to O(n)

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests a harder variant of partition DP where each block's value depends on its range (max-min). It requires careful state design, precomputation of subarray values, and backtracking to output exact k non-overlapping blocks.

## Key Concepts
- 2D DP over prefix index and number of blocks
- Precomputing block values V[l][r] = max - min for all subarrays
- Reconstruction via parent pointers to output endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxRangeSubarrayValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const V = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let mx = -Infinity, mn = Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      mx = Math.max(mx, A[r]);
      mn = Math.min(mn, A[r]);
      V[l][r] = mx - mn;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j - 1][t - 1] + V[j - 1][i - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          parent[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && parent[i][t] !== -1) {
    const j = parent[i][t];
    blocks.push([j, i]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks: blocks.reverse() };
}
```

